        "original_id": "3fce65a1-c456-5ba1-ab43-ef4142fad4e6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Meriwether Lewis, William Clark, Otto Schumann\n- Monuments: Lewis and Clark Memorial Column\n- Expeditions: Lewis and Clark Expedition, Corps of Discovery\n- Places: Washington Park, Portland, Oregon\n- Roles: explorer, soldier, politician, public administrator, artist\n\nFacts:\n- Meriwether Lewis was born on August 18, 1774, and died on October 11, 1809.\n- Meriwether Lewis was an American explorer, soldier, politician, and public administrator.\n- Meriwether Lewis was best known as a leader of the Lewis and Clark Expedition, also called the Corps of Discovery, with William Clark.\n- Otto Schumann was the artist of the Lewis and Clark Memorial Column.\n- The Lewis and Clark Memorial Column is an outdoor monument dedicated to Meriwether Lewis and William Clark for their expedition.\n- The Lewis and Clark Memorial Column is located at Washington Park in Portland, Oregon.",
